sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Reseller as Merchant's server
    participant Guard as merchants.auth.merchant_auth (FastAPI dependency)
    participant Redis as Redis (ip_guard.hit_counter)
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant Route as /merchant/v1 endpoint

    Note over Reseller: signing_key = sha256_hex(secret), derived once at startup<br/>signature = hex(HMAC_SHA256(signing_key, "{ts}\nMETHOD\n/path\n{body}"))
    Reseller->>Guard: X-Merchant-Key, X-Merchant-Timestamp, X-Merchant-Signature + body
    Guard->>Redis: INCR auth:ipguard:merchant-api:{ip} (600/60s)
    alt over the IP ceiling
        Guard-->>Reseller: 429 -- charged BEFORE any parsing, so a flood costs one INCR
    end
    Guard->>Guard: headers present? (401 missing_credentials)
    Guard->>Guard: timestamp integer and within +/-300s? (401 stale_timestamp)
    Guard->>DB: SELECT merchant_api_keys JOIN merchants WHERE key_id = ?
    Note over Guard: signing key = row.secret_hash when the key exists and is not revoked,<br/>otherwise a constant DUMMY -- the HMAC is computed and compared either way,<br/>so timing does not reveal whether the key id exists
    Guard->>Guard: compare_digest(expected, provided)
    alt unknown key OR revoked OR mismatch
        Guard-->>Reseller: 401 invalid_credentials -- one identical body for all three
    end
    Guard->>Redis: INCR merchants:apikey:{key_id} (600/60s) -- only now that it is authenticated
    alt over the per-key ceiling
        Guard-->>Reseller: 429
    end
    alt merchant.status = frozen
        Guard-->>Reseller: 403 merchant_frozen
    else ip_allowlist set and client_ip not in it
        Guard-->>Reseller: 403 ip_not_allowed
    end
    Guard->>DB: UPDATE last_used_at (best effort, at most once a minute per key)
    Guard-->>Route: the authenticated Merchant row (a real UUID, loaded from the DB)
    Route-->>Reseller: 200
